# Component Development Standards

Follow `docs/components/component-architecture.md`.

Rules:

- Components must have one clear responsibility.
- Keep props small, explicit and predictable.
- Prefer composition over abstraction.
- Create shared UI only after real reuse, usually in two or more sections.
- `components/ui` cannot import sections, section data, integrations, env vars or Figma-specific assets.
- Complex sections use a folder with `index.ts`, `{Section}Section.tsx`, subcomponents and `{section}.data.ts`.
- Section data lists belong in local `*.data.ts` files.
- Section complex public API exports through local `index.ts`.
- Prefer semantic HTML: `section`, `article`, `nav`, `dl`, `button`, `a`.
- New or significantly changed reusable components must update `docs/components/README.md`.
